   "operational_classification": "post-provider resource ownership, watchdog establishment and verified teardown",
   "what": "All-stage initialization-core consolidation and core/application separation: relocate reusable implementation from aadistill.init and aadistill.autoinit into aadistill.initialization; extract model-instance and experiment-instance policy into configs and experiment scripts; replace import-time adapter registration with explicit application bootstrap; update current callers and executable dependency closures while preserving mathematical behavior and historical evidence.",
   "why_the_owner_is_shared_session_runner": "The Phase-B executable set and the C1 harness share infrastructure modules,\nso a relocation of those modules moves both identities at once. The shared\nowner is the initialization package boundary itself rather than any one\nphase: aadistill.init and aadistill.autoinit were the shared root, and the\nconsolidation replaces them with aadistill.initialization for every consumer.",
   "why_a_c1_only_override_was_rejected": "This is not a C1 override. C1's launch compatibility is unchanged and remains\nfalse: C1_HARNESS_SOURCE_FILES_V1 is deliberately not repointed and still\nrefuses to produce a digest, and C1's live identity is the separately derived\nexecutable closure. This amendment records movement in the Phase-B executable\nsource set only, and confers nothing on C1.",
   "maintainer_authorization": "MAINTAINER P12 DECISION, 2026-09-08:\n\nThe non-additive all-stage initialization package relocation on\nmigration/initialization-milestone-a is approved for historical accounting.\n\nHistorical preregistrations, raw results, replay digests, grants,\nauthorizations and scientific observations remain immutable. No historical\nexperiment may be described as having run the relocated implementation.\nOld grants and authorizations remain unusable against the migrated tree.\n\nThis approval records current-code movement only. It authorizes no\nexperiment, no GPU/provider resource, no Attempt-10 grant or authorization,\nno scientific field change and no reinterpretation of prior results.",
