   "operational_classification": "post-provider resource ownership, watchdog establishment and verified teardown",
   "what": "Milestone-A merge-review closure on the same branch: move the last repository/application path literals and the remaining semantic experiment policy out of the reusable core. governance/authorization.py keeps only generic authorization, source-binding and budget mechanism (ActionPolicy supplies allowed actions and wire claims; absence of permission remains fail-closed); governance/post_freeze.py takes its note, setup-script and preregistration paths from the caller; infrastructure/session_runner.py executes the commands a SessionSpec carries rather than repository script names it knows; initialization/planning/recovery.py keeps the mechanisms and none of this study's seeds, capability names, thresholds or source lists; runtime/pod_environment.py takes its record path and named files from the application layer. Also: the CUDA validation harness now executes attention.activation_importance_v1 through materialize_fixed_path_suffix, and one stale internal caller of dispatch_branch_hashes was repaired.",
   "why_the_owner_is_shared_session_runner": "These files are shared infrastructure: Phase B's frozen executable set names them, and so do Phase A's, the preflight's and C1's. A change to session_runner.py, session.py, authorization.py or post_freeze.py therefore moves Phase B's live digest even though the change was made for the Milestone-A separation and Phase B is closed. The drift is accounted here rather than hidden, exactly as PHB-HA-001 and PHB-HA-002 accounted theirs.",
   "why_a_c1_only_override_was_rejected": "This confers nothing on C1. C1_HARNESS_SOURCE_FILES_V1 still names pre-migration paths and refuses outright; the repointed declarations fail by digest mismatch. No grant, authorization or bundle is live, and this entry asserts launch_compatible_with_frozen_preregistration: false like every other.",
   "maintainer_authorization": "MAINTAINER MERGE REVIEW DECISION, 2026-09-09, on branch tip dc566fce7b1b8e2d7fac1ade359af2846108aeb3 against public base 4f7b38be: the branch is green and contains a real initialization cutover but is NOT mergeable, for four stated reasons. The decision directs the ownership changes above on the SAME branch, forbids rebasing, squashing, force-pushing or rewriting the existing 43 commits, and directs: 'Use the already-approved source-relocation accounting. Do not modify historical preregistrations, results, grants, authorizations or replay digests. Append only additional relocation/accounting entries.' No Attempt-10 grant, formal authorization, formal bundle or formal experiment is authorized.",
